{
  "requirement": "When implementation shows that agreed requirement text must change, the `habeas-requirements` skill MUST direct agents to stop work that depends on the change and take the changed requirements through review, agreement, and commit before continuing.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement has one obligation. The `habeas-requirements` skill MUST tell agents that when implementation shows agreed text must change, they stop dependent work and take the changed requirements through review, agreement, and commit before continuing.\n\n`tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_requirements_skill_stops_dependent_work_when_agreed_text_must_change]` covers it in two ways:\n- It asserts, through `assert_phrases` and `bundled_skill` (which build the skill text from `SKILL.md` and its reference files), that the skill contains \"If implementation shows that agreed text must change, stop work that depends on it and take the changed requirements through steps 3 to 5 first\". That sentence has the trigger, the instruction to stop dependent work, and the \"before continuing\" ordering.\n- It checks that the referenced steps are the right ones. Using `step`, which reads the numbered Workflow steps via `workflow_steps`, it asserts that step 3 starts with \"Review.\", step 4 with \"Present\" (agreement) and step 5 with \"Commit.\". So \"steps 3 to 5\" means review, agreement and commit.\n\nThe assertions fail if the sentence is removed or reworded, or if the step numbering drifts. The test is marked `{test}` for the subject. I found no unmarked relevant tests and no uncovered obligations.",
